Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.17,0:00:07.86,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,We made it...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.86,0:00:09.35,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Your knees okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.35,0:00:11.36,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,I think so...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.85,0:00:11.36,Alderamin-overlap,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Hey, you guys!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.84,0:00:13.74,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,What are you doing here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.74,0:00:18.99,sign_330_6_Alafatra_Mountai,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Alafatra Mountain Range \N3800 meters above sea level
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.65,0:00:17.92,Alderamin-top,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,This is the front lines... the very front!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.04,0:01:53.96,Alderamin-Episode_Title,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(650,1)}The Fate of a Small Honor
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.60,0:02:00.14,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,So, things are bad enough \Nthat you're being sent here?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.97,0:02:02.80,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,Um, First Lieutenant?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.80,0:02:06.04,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Actually, it's "Captain" now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.04,0:02:07.89,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Just provisionally, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.26,0:02:10.15,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,My apologies, Captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.45,0:02:14.20,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,Would you tell us\Nthe current state of the war?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.20,0:02:15.15,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.96,0:02:18.89,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We're nearing the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.89,0:02:24.30,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Three forces are heading to fight\Nthe Sinack via separate mountain routes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.30,0:02:26.50,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,When the enemy splits up,\Nwe whittle them down,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.50,0:02:28.91,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,then meet up on the ground at the other side.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.51,0:02:33.66,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Therefore driving the enemy\N into a single, decisive battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.66,0:02:37.39,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,That's Lieutenant General Safida's plan, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.39,0:02:39.54,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Um, Captain Sazaluf,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.54,0:02:40.68,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,may I ask a few things?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.23,0:02:45.19,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,No pointing out fundamental \Nproblems with the plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.19,0:02:46.93,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Too late for that now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.28,0:02:49.69,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You've made it this far.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.72,0:02:53.47,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We've got lots of safe jobs for you to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.47,0:02:57.87,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I know. I'll combine all five of\N your platoons into one company.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.87,0:03:01.57,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Warrant Officer Ikta, from now \Non you're company commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.57,0:03:02.32,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.75,0:03:04.89,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Right, got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.89,0:03:07.83,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,So what, exactly, should we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.26,0:03:10.58,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,First, the simple job of \Nstarting the bonfires.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.58,0:03:12.29,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Don't let their whining get to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.27,0:03:22.57,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,As if killing us and\Nstealing from us wasn't enough,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.57,0:03:24.09,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,now you burn our homes?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.94,0:03:26.47,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You are monsters!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.29,0:03:29.89,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Ah, please wait a little longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.89,0:03:34.36,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,As soon as the flames go out,\Nwe'll take you to a village to the west.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.84,0:03:40.29,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Looks like I underestimated Captain Sazaluf.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.75,0:03:45.23,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Especially his sense of humor,\Nif he's calling arson "lighting bonfires."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.23,0:03:48.37,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,This was better than it \Ncould have been, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.80,0:03:52.90,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,What if we'd been ordered to kill them?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.90,0:03:58.02,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,That would've been the plan\Nif the Captain hadn't spoken up.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.80,0:04:02.87,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,He's burning their villages and \Nisolating the people in another area.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.87,0:04:04.96,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,He's cutting off the enemy's supply source,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.96,0:04:07.10,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,and he can use them for negotiations.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.88,0:04:12.55,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,It's a hell of a lot better than Lieutenant \NGeneral Safida's haphazard strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.55,0:04:15.60,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I was shocked when I saw that map.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.63,0:04:20.59,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,All the routes we're following are \Nseparated by over 100 kilometers.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.21,0:04:23.32,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,The forces can't help one another,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.32,0:04:26.30,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,and it's clear we're going to see\Na lot of deserters.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.30,0:04:28.53,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,It's a massive failure as a strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.47,0:04:33.89,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,And to make matters worse, not only are \Nwe paying the price for these mistakes,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.89,0:04:35.83,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,but so are the Sinack.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.84,0:04:40.17,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Unlike this area, where the Captain's\Nplan was put into effect,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.17,0:04:43.28,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,everyone is being slaughtered\Nin the villages to our rear.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.71,0:04:46.89,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Nothing about this is scientific.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.38,0:04:49.50,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,It's a ridiculous war.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.72,0:04:53.73,sign_6971_61_Sinack_Village_R,I,0000,0000,0000,,Sinack Village Refugee Camp
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.25,0:04:53.73,Alderamin-top,I,0000,0000,0000,,Okay, eight to this house.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.38,0:04:57.65,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,We can have the Sotoi family here,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.65,0:04:59.18,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,and then...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.18,0:04:59.98,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.27,0:05:02.48,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Get lost, imperial dog!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.68,0:05:07.74,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Next, the Gitonko family can go...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.74,0:05:08.49,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Give it back!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.49,0:05:09.99,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Give back our village!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.67,0:05:15.60,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Young man, I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.60,0:05:19.25,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Once this is done, I promise \Nwe'll disappear completely.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.25,0:05:20.75,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Can you let me go?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.78,0:05:42.94,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,What are you doing, you wretch?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.71,0:05:47.11,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Brave boy!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.82,0:05:48.98,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.98,0:05:51.62,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I apologize for my comrade's behavior!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.53,0:05:56.85,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,That nosebleed is a sign that you \Nstood up against something unfair!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.85,0:05:59.04,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,It's something to be proud of!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.04,0:06:00.46,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Splendid!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.88,0:06:04.39,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I punished the man who did this to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.39,0:06:06.11,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,But that is probably not enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.27,0:06:11.95,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Now we match, young hero.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.22,0:06:18.23,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,A-Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.12,0:06:22.76,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,How dare you lay hands on a child?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.76,0:06:25.19,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I'm disgusted with you, Ikta Solork.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.19,0:06:26.50,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,How could you do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.50,0:06:28.24,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,We have our reasons—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.43,0:06:34.17,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You have a problem with it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.17,0:06:35.63,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,No, I don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.98,0:06:38.05,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.33,0:06:41.63,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,While you're at it,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.63,0:06:44.57,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,think you could take care \Nof getting them set up?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.96,0:06:47.04,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I don't think they'll hate you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.70,0:06:49.59,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Of course, gladly, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.42,0:06:51.48,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.21,0:06:57.03,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Why did you back down?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.81,0:07:01.10,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Making a child bleed was my mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.10,0:07:04.21,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Warrant Officer Deinkun handled it for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.21,0:07:05.46,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I should be grateful.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.46,0:07:06.91,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I refuse to accept that!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.91,0:07:09.54,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,We're at war!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.54,0:07:10.92,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Our job is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.67,0:07:13.62,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,to kill lots of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.24,0:07:17.87,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,He should be doing the same thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.05,0:07:21.62,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,It's hypocrisy!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.88,0:07:26.96,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Hey, Suya, if you think \Nunconditional kindness is good,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.96,0:07:31.10,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,and any sort of kindness that comes\N with conditions is hypocrisy,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.10,0:07:33.26,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,you should reconsider.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.51,0:07:39.14,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,People can only achieve\Nas much as the situation allows.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.63,0:07:41.27,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.11,0:07:45.76,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,We have to kill the ones who fight us,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.38,0:07:50.28,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,but I want to take care of the ones \Nwho aren't fighting us as best I can.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.06,0:07:53.73,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Warrant Officer Deinkun's just like us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.73,0:07:56.28,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,It hurts him to fight our comrades.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.28,0:07:57.75,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,The same?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.75,0:07:59.69,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,You had rocks thrown at you
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.69,0:08:01.66,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,and got punched so hard,\Nyour face is swollen!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.63,0:08:04.27,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Sorry, Suya.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.27,0:08:06.17,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I just choose the right one for the job.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.84,0:08:11.80,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Warrant Officer Deinkun's \Na real knight, not like me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.63,0:08:16.19,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,He shouldn't be doing the jobs \Nthat make people hate him, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.06,0:08:22.02,sign_11990_121_Several_Days_Lat,I,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(1,550)}Several Days Later \NCamp, 4200 meters above sea level
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.79,0:08:25.65,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The end of the battle draws near!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.13,0:08:29.19,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The remaining Sinack forces \Nare gathering in a large village
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.19,0:08:31.65,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,on the other side of this canyon!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.65,0:08:34.91,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,That will probably be the \Nlocation of the last battle!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.91,0:08:36.09,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I ask you to fight hard
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.09,0:08:41.41,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,and make their blood an offering to those \N who have fallen here on Great Alafatra!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.83,0:08:44.00,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We leave in the morning,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.00,0:08:47.66,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,so for tonight, rest up for the last battle!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.66,0:08:49.17,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Dismissed!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.18,0:08:56.30,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,The average age here looks a lot \Nyounger than when we started.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.69,0:08:58.33,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Of course it does.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.33,0:09:00.86,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,We started with 18,000 men in three brigades.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.86,0:09:02.68,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Now we've got less than half of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.51,0:09:05.50,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,And most died from altitude sickness,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.50,0:09:07.19,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,not wounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.75,0:09:09.59,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Completely ridiculous.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.87,0:09:13.57,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Haro, want to go wipe ourselves down?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.57,0:09:15.60,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,We can use hot water tonight, it seems.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.38,0:09:17.82,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,That sounds great.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.82,0:09:19.33,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,I'll go with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.37,0:09:27.21,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Hey, I wanted to ask you something...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.21,0:09:29.08,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,What is it, Ma-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.20,0:09:34.42,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,How do you handle them during the war?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.42,0:09:36.74,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,I mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.74,0:09:39.95,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,your... needs.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.70,0:09:43.46,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Matthew, my friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.46,0:09:47.37,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,That question divides us \Ninto two types of people.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.37,0:09:49.46,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Heroes who rely on bonds with others,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.46,0:09:51.73,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,or warriors who live in solitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.05,0:09:54.60,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,That's quite the metaphor.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.60,0:09:56.24,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Torway, which are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.66,0:09:58.03,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,A hero or a warrior?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.78,0:10:01.99,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,I-I don't really...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.99,0:10:03.93,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Cut him some slack, Matthew.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.93,0:10:08.19,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Hotties like him are usually\Nstubborn warriors.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.19,0:10:10.19,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Yeah, maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.19,0:10:12.63,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,But the question here is about you, Ikta.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.91,0:10:16.50,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Intercourse during wartime, \Nboth hetero- and homosexual,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.50,0:10:18.63,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,is against military regulations.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.63,0:10:21.37,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Why are you, of all people, \Nbringing up regulations?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.37,0:10:24.38,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,From what you just said, I bet \Nyou're doing it with somebody.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.38,0:10:25.42,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Who is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.42,0:10:26.66,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Someone from your platoon?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.66,0:10:29.15,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Come on, even I know better than that—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.15,0:10:30.44,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Another platoon, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.85,0:10:34.02,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,No, maybe it's more realistic \Nto assume it's another officer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.02,0:10:36.15,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Could it be Yatori or Haro?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.54,0:10:41.14,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Matthew, can you imagine an Igsem \Nfamily heir breaking military regulations?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.14,0:10:43.28,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,And Haro's a lot more proper than she looks.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.97,0:10:47.04,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Good to see you've got lots of energy,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.54,0:10:50.04,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,but if you're gonna talk \Nabout that, keep it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.04,0:10:52.25,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,I-I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.25,0:10:54.29,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,This is embarrassing, Ma-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.29,0:10:56.45,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,So sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.45,0:10:59.05,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,By the way, how are you \Nhandling it, Captain Sazaluf?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.31,0:11:01.80,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,A former hero, I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.80,0:11:03.30,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Not that I can talk about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.53,0:11:05.37,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,As I'd expect from an elder.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.37,0:11:08.33,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,When we get back to base,\Ntell me the stories of your glory.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.33,0:11:09.81,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Some day.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.44,0:11:13.66,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Jeez, that sucked.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.66,0:11:15.24,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Let's go back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.24,0:11:17.44,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,So, my friend Matthew, what about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.48,0:11:21.82,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,It's not fair to just run away, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.23,0:11:24.83,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Now, tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.59,0:11:26.83,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Are you a hero?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.45,0:11:28.83,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Or a warrior?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.96,0:11:36.25,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,P-Pay your respects to a lonely warrior!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.41,0:11:40.26,Default,All,0000,0000,0000,,Sir, yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.05,0:11:54.79,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I don't like this terrain.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.79,0:12:01.24,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,Um, are you worried about air mortars\Nbeing fired from the other side?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.99,0:12:06.47,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,If they were to just line up and\N start firing, we'd be helpless.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.47,0:12:10.41,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,That's a legitimate concern, \Nbut I don't think it's likely.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.25,0:12:12.60,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.28,0:12:16.88,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,It wouldn't be easy to get mortars up there.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.60,0:12:19.92,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,And if they had,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.92,0:12:22.26,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,we would be able to see it from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.91,0:12:26.32,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,But there's no sign of them, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.32,0:12:27.60,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.60,0:12:31.22,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,No, Captain Sazaluf. Better safe than sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.01,0:12:35.52,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Why don't we put shields on the side \Nof the officer candidates unit?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.54,0:12:39.85,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,What he just said actually convinced me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.85,0:12:41.53,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I feel the same,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.21,0:12:44.41,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,but it may not be cannonballs we're facing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.50,0:12:49.56,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,Captain, I take back my earlier words.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.56,0:12:55.18,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,Would you give the order to \Nprotect our flank with shields?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.18,0:12:57.36,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Are you serious?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.36,0:13:00.53,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,That means we'd have to get off our horses.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.53,0:13:03.30,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,So would Lieutenant\N General Safida over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.30,0:13:04.81,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.81,0:13:09.51,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,And the highest-ranking officer \Nwho can make that proposal is...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.93,0:13:12.29,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.29,0:13:15.44,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You want me off my horse?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.26,0:13:20.77,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Um, I know this will be an additional \Nstrain on you, Lieutenant General.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.77,0:13:22.69,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I'm very sorry, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.23,0:13:24.95,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We should prepare for an attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.16,0:13:30.58,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Too much caution is no \Ndifferent than cowardice.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.90,0:13:37.03,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I'm so lame.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.69,0:13:39.83,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Captain Senpa Sazaluf?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.46,0:13:43.60,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,May I say one thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.60,0:13:46.80,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Oh, god... now what?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.32,0:13:49.66,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,You are the best superior \Nofficer we could have.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.66,0:13:52.22,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I thank you from the bottom of my heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.99,0:14:00.45,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Don't tease your elders, guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.51,0:14:03.29,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,That was the flash signal.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.29,0:14:04.61,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The attack is beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.04,0:14:10.87,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Our only target is Tamtooktsk Safida, \NCommander of the Northern Garrison.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.59,0:14:15.15,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We'll go under the cover of the Sinack \Nattack and complete our mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.15,0:14:17.36,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Once again, no casualties are permitted.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.36,0:14:21.86,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Be prepared to dive into the canyon, \Nbut only if you cannot avoid it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.86,0:14:24.13,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We cannot shame ourselves by leaving corpses.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.97,0:14:26.78,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Begin the operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.60,0:14:29.76,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Kala Karm, heading out.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.81,0:14:35.56,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Enemy attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.72,0:14:38.81,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,The mountains are our world!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.81,0:14:42.31,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Watch and be amazed, demons of the plains!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.82,0:14:45.12,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,D-Directly above?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.12,0:14:47.89,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,How did they get troops directly above us?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.89,0:14:49.19,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Calm down, Matthew.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.19,0:14:51.57,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,They've been pushed to the brink\Nand into a desperate attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.57,0:14:52.55,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.55,0:14:54.15,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,As long as we can stay calm...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.33,0:14:57.31,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Gunfire?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.31,0:14:58.26,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,From above?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.26,0:14:59.96,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,No! From the other side!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.96,0:15:00.84,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.84,0:15:01.76,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The other side?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.76,0:15:02.83,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Don't be stupid!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.83,0:15:04.65,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,That's 200 meters away!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.65,0:15:06.28,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Air guns can't shoot that far—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.28,0:15:08.23,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Ikkun, they've got them, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.23,0:15:10.34,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,That's right. They're using air rifles.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.76,0:15:13.29,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Torway, hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.29,0:15:16.37,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Your men are the only ones with air rifles!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.37,0:15:19.16,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,Roger! I'll put down suppressing fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.16,0:15:21.10,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,I'll protect Lieutenant General Safida!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.15,0:15:24.12,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,From above!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.12,0:15:24.98,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,They're coming down!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.98,0:15:26.61,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Ready bayonets!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.07,0:15:28.85,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,I can't get it to fit!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.85,0:15:30.11,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Haro, above!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.15,0:15:37.91,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I'm here to help!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.40,0:15:43.85,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Stand up, Ikta Solork.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.85,0:15:46.42,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Even I'm not saving you a second time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.12,0:15:49.84,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Thanks, Warrant Officer Deinkun,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.84,0:15:51.93,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,but this {\i1}is{\i0} the second time you've saved me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.52,0:15:54.71,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,What happened at the village doesn't count.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.71,0:15:57.99,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Sorry for damaging your honor back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.99,0:15:59.86,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.86,0:16:04.06,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I never had honor that could be damaged by\Na punch to the face and time on the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.84,0:16:08.82,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,What would damage it, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.82,0:16:18.23,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Being unable to say what I wanted, \Nwhen I wanted to say it,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.90,0:16:22.75,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,or being unable to protect someone \Nwhen I wanted to protect them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.23,0:16:29.25,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Probably something like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.14,0:16:31.61,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I don't understand that,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.61,0:16:33.51,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,but I do understand one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.88,0:16:35.39,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You and I are very different.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.83,0:16:38.11,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,However, in the end...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.82,0:16:41.52,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You're a knight, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.77,0:16:58.24,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Lieutenant General Safida, \Nplease do not move from there.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.84,0:17:02.32,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,We meet again, Red One.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.32,0:17:05.97,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,I feel lucky for this opportunity, \Nchieftain of the Sinack.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.86,0:17:09.15,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,I'm Warrant Officer Yatorishino Igsem\Nof the Army.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.75,0:17:11.72,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,My partner is the fire spirit Shia.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.68,0:17:15.07,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I am Nanaku Daru, chieftain of the Sinack.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.07,0:17:16.64,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,My Hahashiku is Hisha of the Wind.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.13,0:17:18.68,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I'll give you my name,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.68,0:17:20.64,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,but I won't bother remembering your rank.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.21,0:17:22.83,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,That's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.83,0:17:26.15,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Just remember the feeling\Nof my blade as you die!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.47,0:17:27.90,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.17,0:17:43.79,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,What's wrong, Red One?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.79,0:17:45.16,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Can't even fight back?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.36,0:17:48.79,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Y,0000,0000,0000,,What an unorthodox method...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.43,0:17:50.95,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Rule-breaking, but beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.55,0:17:53.05,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Stop already!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.42,0:17:55.13,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,No, I won't!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.61,0:17:57.93,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,A horizontal to vertical spin?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.93,0:17:59.64,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Bingo!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.39,0:18:04.68,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,From the other side again?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.68,0:18:05.44,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.44,0:18:06.64,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,From below the cliff!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.38,0:18:08.40,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,They're...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.72,0:18:09.90,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Impertinence...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.27,0:18:12.15,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I'll defeat them!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.15,0:18:13.07,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Don't rush in!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.07,0:18:15.32,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,They're different from the others!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.21,0:18:18.43,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I'm amazed you withstood that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.43,0:18:20.32,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,It was taking all I've got.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.00,0:18:22.57,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,But that's enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.57,0:18:24.20,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I've learned your techniques.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.46,0:18:25.57,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Learned my techniques?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.57,0:18:26.71,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Silence!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.71,0:18:29.63,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Regret your arrogance in the next world!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.38,0:18:35.63,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,There won't be a second time!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.87,0:18:36.92,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,You fell for it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.09,0:18:42.01,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,That pea shooter won't be enough...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.46,0:18:58.15,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,How... did you...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.15,0:19:00.20,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,How did I find out about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.52,0:19:06.20,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Several things didn't add up.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.37,0:19:09.90,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,You didn't seem to be \Ncarrying a spirit with you,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.36,0:19:12.82,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,but you gave his name anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.16,0:19:15.91,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,That was all?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.91,0:19:16.92,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.92,0:19:20.98,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,What really made me notice \Nwas the bold way you fought.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.65,0:19:26.27,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Every swordswoman knows better \Nthan to leave her back exposed.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.27,0:19:28.24,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,That's why I was sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.24,0:19:30.52,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,You had something up your sleeve.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.67,0:19:33.37,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Hisha, was it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.37,0:19:35.25,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Move and I'll kill your mistress.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.86,0:19:38.62,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,The battle is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.62,0:19:41.66,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Tell your tribe to surrender, Nanaku Daru.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.91,0:19:47.71,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,What are you...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.08,0:19:51.25,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Nana, live!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.18,0:19:56.34,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Hisha!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.71,0:19:59.20,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Warrant Officer Deinkun!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.36,0:20:19.86,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Matthew Platoon, surround them!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.69,0:20:31.01,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,We let her get away, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.36,0:20:36.46,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Dein! Dein!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.94,0:20:38.33,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Don't die!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.65,0:20:43.33,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Yatori, you do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.12,0:21:02.41,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,What did he say?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.09,0:21:05.80,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,"Take care of my comrades in the Empire."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.10,0:21:08.83,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,And he asked me a question.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.56,0:21:14.08,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,"Was I able to uphold my honor as a knight?"
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.62,0:21:17.25,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,What did you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.74,0:21:25.37,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Deinkun Hargunska fought \Nmore bravely than anyone,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.37,0:21:27.65,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,and loved the Empire and his comrades.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.22,0:21:31.12,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Glory and blessings be upon his soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.42,0:21:35.91,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Hisha, I'm sorry...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.91,0:21:39.22,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I'm sorry I couldn't even \Npick up your Soulstone.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.57,0:21:41.90,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I'll make those demons pay.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.90,0:21:44.31,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Just wait, everyone...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.31,0:21:48.14,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Grandma, Grandpa, I'm coming home...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.15,0:21:59.33,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Narr,0000,0000,0000,,August, Imperial Year 906.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.33,0:22:02.23,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Narr,0000,0000,0000,,The madness of the war deepened
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.23,0:22:04.92,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Narr,0000,0000,0000,,and continued to spiral out of control.
